    <item>
      <title>Sparing use of phosphorus in an acidifying ocean</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41561-026-02133-8</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Geoscience, Published online: 05 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41561-026-02133-8"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41561-026-02133-8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Global cycles of carbon and phosphorus decouple under intensifying ocean acidification as marine diatoms restructure their lipid membranes and downregulate organic phosphorus scavenging to adapt to the decreasing pH.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>Sparing use of phosphorus in an acidifying ocean</dc:title>
